# Turning and looking out at the colossi must never make one pop, clip or
# vanish (src/render/colossus/colossus_view.gd does its own culling on angles,
# because the engine cannot see where a compressed vertex really is). The staged
# eye turns thirty degrees a second past the skyline walker and the looming one,
# and consecutive frames are shot: a walker that is cut by the culling, or
# clipped by the far plane, shows as a frame that disagrees with its neighbours.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_turn.tour --seed=7 --place=coast --hour=12 --face=300 --eye=1.7,-5 --eye-turn=30 --weather=clear:0
wait 6
shot turn-00
wait 0.2
shot turn-01
wait 0.2
shot turn-02
wait 0.2
shot turn-03
wait 0.2
shot turn-04
wait 0.2
shot turn-05
wait 0.2
shot turn-06
wait 0.2
shot turn-07
wait 0.2
shot turn-08
wait 0.2
shot turn-09
wait 0.2
shot turn-10
wait 0.2
shot turn-11
wait 0.2
shot turn-12
wait 0.2
shot turn-13
wait 0.2
shot turn-14
wait 0.2
shot turn-15
wait 0.2
shot turn-16
